#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:2
msgid "Running tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:5
msgid "An example task"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:7
msgid ""
"Poe tasks are defined in your **pyproject.toml** file under ``tool.poe."
"tasks``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:9
msgid ""
"The following toml example defines a task called `test` that consists of the "
"associated command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:11
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"test = \"pytest --cov=poethepoet\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:16
msgid "This task can the be run via the poe cli as ``poe test``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:20
msgid ""
"If your pyproject defines pytest as a dependency with poetry, then poe will "
"run the task with pytest from the poetry managed virtualenv, so you don't "
"need to explicitly activate the virtualenv via ``poetry shell`` or ``poetry "
"run``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:23
msgid ""
"`Click here for a real example <https://github.com/nat-n/poethepoet/blob/"
"main/pyproject.toml>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:27
msgid "Run a task with the poe CLI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:29
msgid "The preferred way to run poe is via the standalone CLI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:31
msgid "poe test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:35
msgid ""
"The above command can only be ran if you've :doc:`installed Poe globally<../"
"installation>`, or if you've sourced the venv that Poe the Poet is installed "
"in (e.g. using ``poetry shell``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:39
msgid "Running Poe as a Python module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:41
msgid "You can also run poe as a python module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:43
msgid "python -m poethepoet [options] test [task_args]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:49
msgid "Running Poe as a Poetry plugin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:50
msgid ""
"If you've installed it as a :doc:`poetry plugin<../poetry_plugin>` (for "
"poetry >= 1.2), you can run it like so"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:52
msgid ""
"poetry self add poethepoet[poetry_plugin]\n"
"poetry poe [options] test [task_args]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:59
msgid "Running Poe as a Poetry dependency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:60
msgid ""
"If you've installed it as a dev dependency with poetry, you can run it like "
"so"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:62
msgid ""
"poetry add --group dev poethepoet\n"
"poetry run poe [options] test [task_args]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:69
msgid ""
"In this case you might want create an alias like :sh:`alias poe='poetry run "
"poe'`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:73
msgid "Passing arguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:75
msgid "By default additional arguments are passed to the task so"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:77
msgid "poe test -v tests/favorite_test.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:81
msgid "will result in the following being run inside poetry's virtualenv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/running_guide.rst:83
msgid "pytest --cov=poethepoet -v tests/favorite_test.py"
msgstr ""
